# Input graph for emmo-repo__domain-electrochemistry__.github_scripts_check_iri_resolution.py__ontology_subject
# -- written during translation.
#
# Several solutions of the pattern the region reads (onto1, onto2: both
# `a owl:Ontology`) -- the region returns whichever the store yields first,
# so a translation that changed the traversal order would show up here.
# Neighbourhood that must NOT match: onto3 is typed with a different class
# that merely shares the local name "Ontology"; describes--owl:imports-->onto1
# puts owl:Ontology-shaped data in a position (object of owl:imports) that a
# too-broad pattern could pick up by mistake.
#
# The zero-solution case (no owl:Ontology triple at all) is NOT encoded as a
# second fixture/call here: the region does not return None on that path, it
# raises RuntimeError -- and rdfeval.harness.run_pair treats any exception
# raised by the entry point as a fatal harness error (it aborts the whole
# comparison, `verdict["error"]`), not as a value to compare, so there is no
# way to drive that branch through `rdfeval check` without producing a
# spurious FAIL. Confirmed by hand instead (see meta.json translation_notes):
# both original.py and translated.ldpy raise RuntimeError with the identical
# message for an empty graph.
@prefix ex: <http://example.org/> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .

ex:onto1 a owl:Ontology .
ex:onto2 a owl:Ontology .

# neighbour that must NOT match: same local name, different vocabulary
ex:onto3 a ex:Ontology .

# neighbour that must NOT match: owl:Ontology-shaped data in object position
ex:describes owl:imports ex:onto1 .
